<mujoco model="liftdrop_tower">
  <!--
    LiftDrop at Halden Tower: the lobby (four shop units and the security desk), level 20 and
    level 23, joined by a glass lift. Floors 21 and 22 aren't modelled: storeys are 3.2 m, so L20 is
    at z 3.2 and L23 at z 6.4. Metres, z up, lobby floor at z=0.
    The robot never enters an office: on L20 and L23 it parks in the painted bay outside the
    security gate (1.85, 1.15), and the customer comes out to it.

    Collision bits: world = 1, lift car = 2, robot conaffinity = 3 (touches both).
    The car and the world never collide, so the car passes through the slabs' shaft holes and
    sits flush with each floor.

    Layout (x east, y north), camera looking north-east from the south-west:
      lobby   dock (1,-2) · restaurants along y=3..7.5 (pickup windows on y=3): café 0.1, bakery -1.95, noodles -4, greens -6.05
              security desk (-1.8,-2) · security office x -7..-4.4, y -5..-2.6 · lift (4.5, 0)
      L20/L23 slab x 1..7 · gate line y=1.6 (speed gate x 2.4..3.4) · desks behind, y 2..5
-->
  <compiler autolimits="true"/>
  <option timestep="0.002"/>
  <visual>
    <global offwidth="1280" offheight="720"/>
    <headlight ambient="0.35 0.35 0.35" diffuse="0.5 0.5 0.5"/>
  </visual>

  <asset>
